### Changed

- Integrate the complete M9 frontend redesign into `main` and add the v1.9.0 release notes. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Add numbered inline citation badges to sanitized assistant Markdown and keep citations without an inline match in the sources list. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Render the first actionable `SuggestedNextSteps` item as the primary ticket control, with remaining steps in the overflow menu. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operable `CommandPalette` to `MainLayout`, opened with Ctrl/Cmd+K and populated from `NavRegistry` and debounced, cancellable ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Update ticket status optimistically on the board and detail views, reconciling successful board moves and restoring the prior state when a transition is rejected. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace status and assignee dialogs with inline `MudMenu` popovers that apply changes without navigation. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Anchor assistant citations inline with `AnswerCitationLayout`, leaving citations without a title match in the sources list. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Include the active agent roster in each chat system prompt using `GetAgentsHandler`. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Require `check_grounding` through `tool_choice` once after passages are retrieved and before the first answer token is streamed. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Centralize the palette, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors in `Theme/DesignTokens.cs` and use the tokens across stylesheets and `AppTheme`. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Wrap the board card title link in `board-card__title-row` so the title clamps to two lines instead of expanding the card. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Apply the assistant panel styles through `::deep .assistant-chat` so the composer stays inset within the panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Give the `Category` column a 140px width and use the uppercase label style to prevent its header from overlapping `Due`. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Require a successful tool result before claiming a write succeeded, and avoid reconfirming requested changes except when a genuine decision or missing information requires it. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Convert ticket summary timestamps to `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` before including them in the model prompt. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Mark caught `search_knowledge_base` failures as errors while preserving unavailable results as non-errors. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Score substantive answer sentences against retrieved passages by embedding similarity, retaining `LexicalGroundingEvaluator` as the fallback. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
